course: dictionary
lesson: 16020
title: Velocity: speed with a direction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Speed tells you how fast something moves. Velocity tells you how fast and which way. «The car drove at 20 metres per second towards the school.» The speed is 20 metres per second, and the direction is towards the school, so that is its velocity.
explain: In everyday talk, velocity can just mean speed, especially high speed. «The velocity of the train made the leaves swirl.» But in science lessons, velocity always includes a direction, and it is measured in metres per second (m/s).
explain: Direction matters. If you run round a track at the same speed, your speed stays the same, but your velocity keeps changing, because your direction keeps changing. To check a word like this, ask: how fast, and which way?
fact: Velocity means speed in a particular direction.
fact: Velocity is measured in metres per second, written m/s.
fact: In everyday use, «velocity» can simply mean high speed.
fact: Speed tells how fast something goes; velocity tells how fast and which way.
fact: Escape velocity is the speed a rocket needs to leave Earth's pull.
exercise: «The ball rolled north at 3 metres per second.» What does the velocity tell us? | How heavy the ball is | Only how far the ball rolled | The colour of the ball | *How fast the ball moved and which way
exercise: Ella says velocity is just a fancy word for speed. What is the best answer? | *Not quite: velocity is speed with a direction | Yes, they mean exactly the same in every case | Velocity is only used for cars | Velocity is a kind of weather
exercise: Which unit is used to measure velocity? | Litres | Kilograms | Hours | *Metres per second (m/s)
test: «The runner kept the same speed around the track, yet her velocity kept changing. Why?» | *Her direction kept changing | Her speed changed a lot | The track was getting shorter | She was getting heavier
test: What is escape velocity? | A slow wind across a field | The speed of a sleeping snail | A way to escape from a maths test | *The speed a rocket needs to leave Earth's pull
exam: «The rocket shot off at high velocity, straight up into the sky.» Which words tell us the direction of the velocity? | the sky | high velocity | *straight up | shot off
